JSON with `name`, `tools`, and nested `hooks`\n26\t- CLI hook names and protocol mapping:\n27\t  | Native Hook Name | When It Fires | Protocol Event Type |\n28\t  |-----------------|---------------|---------------------|\n29\t  | `agentSpawn` | CLI session starts | `SessionStart` |\n30\t  | `userPromptSubmit` | User submits a prompt | `TurnStart` |\n31\t  | `preToolUse` | Before a tool call | no lifecycle event |\n32\t  | `postToolUse` | After a tool call | no lifecycle event |\n33\t  | `stop` | CLI turn ends | `TurnEnd` |\n34\t- CLI hook payload: JSON on stdin with `hook_event_name`, `cwd`, `prompt`, `tool_name`, `tool_input`, and `tool_response`\n35\t- IDE hook config files: `.kiro/hooks/*.kiro.hook`\n36\t- IDE hook config format: JSON with `enabled`, `name`, `description`, `version`, `when`, and `then`\n37\t- IDE trigger types installed by Entire: `promptSubmit`, `agentStop`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`\n38\t- IDE hook input: the adapter tolerates empty stdin and falls back to environment variables such as `USER_PROMPT`\n39\t- IDE hook command form: macOS/Linux use `sh -c '<command> </dev/null'`; Windows emits the bare hook command directly because the adapter already times out empty stdin reads safely\n40\t\n41\t## Session Management\n42\t- Session ID source: `parse-hook` prefers native Kiro identifiers first (hook payload `session_id` / `sessionId` / `conversation_id` / `chatSessionId` when present, then the latest IDE `sessionId`, then the cached Entire session ID, then the CLI `conversation_id`, and only then a generated Entire ID)\n43\t- Session cache lifetime: `.entire/tmp/kiro-active-session` persists across `stop` events so repeated prompts in the same IDE chat tab stay in one Entire session; the cache is replaced when a newer native Kiro session ID is observed\n44\t- Session directory: `.entire/tmp/` under the repo root\n45\t- Session file format: cached JSON transcript, one file per session ID\n46\t- Session file path: `.entire/tmp/<session-id>.json`\n47\t- Native CLI session lookup: SQLite database at `~/Library/Application Support/kiro-cli/data.sqlite3` on macOS, `~/.local/share/kiro-cli/data.sqlite3` on Linux, or `%LOCALAPPDATA%/kiro-cli/data.sqlite3` on Windows\n48\t- Native CLI lookup key: the current working directory is queried against `conversations_v2`\n49\t- Native IDE session lookup: `~/Library/Application Support/Kiro/User/globalStorage/kiro.kiroagent/workspace-sessions/<base64(cwd)>/sessions.json` on macOS, `~/.config/Kiro/User/globalStorage/kiro.kiroagent/workspace-sessions/<base64(cwd)>/sessions.json` on Linux, or `%APPDATA%/Kiro/User/globalStorage/kiro.kiroagent/workspace-sessions/<base64(cwd)>/sessions.json` on Windows\n50\t- IDE transcript source: the most recent entry in `sessions.json`, then `<sessionId>.json` in the same directory\n51\t\n52\t## Transcript\n53\t- CLI transcript format: JSON object with `conversation_id` and `history`\n54\t- CLI history entries: paired user and assistant messages\n55\t- User prompt shape: `history[].user.content` containing a tagged union such as `{\"Prompt\":{\"prompt\":\"...\"}}`\n56\t- Assistant tool-call shape: `history[].assistant` containing `{\"ToolUse\": {...}}`\n57\t- Assistant response shape: `history[].assistant` containing `{\"Response\": {...}}`\n58\t- IDE transcript format: JSON object with `history`, where each entry contains a `message` object\n59\t- IDE message shape: Anthropic-style `role` plus `content`\n60\t- CLI transcript capture: fetched from SQLite at turn end and cached to `.entire/tmp/<session-id>.json`\n61\t- IDE transcript capture: copied from the workspace session file into `.entire/tmp/<session-id>.json`\n62\t\n63\t## Protocol Mapping\n64\t| Subcommand | Native Concept | Implementation Notes | Feasibility |\n65\t|-----------|---------------|---------------------|-------------|\n66\t| `info` | adapter metadata | static JSON describing `kiro` and declared capabilities | Required |\n67\t| `detect` | `.kiro` repository config | presence is inferred from repo-local Kiro state | Required |\n68\t| `get-session-id` | cached stable session ID | use the cached Entire session ID, not Kiro's transient DB state | Required |\n69\t| `get-session-dir` | Entire cache directory | return `<repo>/.entire/tmp` | Required |\n70\t| `resolve-session-file` | normalized cache path | return `<repo>/.entire/tmp/<id>.json` | Required |\n71\t| `read-session` | cached transcript file | read the normalized JSON cache and synthesize `AgentSession` | Required |\n72\t| `write-session` | normalized transcript cache | write the cached transcript back for rewind/resume | Required |\n73\t| `read-transcript` | cached transcript bytes | return raw bytes from `.entire/tmp/<id>.json` | Required |\n74\t| `chunk-transcript` | raw transcript bytes | chunk the cached JSON for transport; no native Kiro format change needed | Required |\n75\t| `reassemble-transcript` | chunk reassembly | reverse `chunk-transcript` | Required |\n76\t| `format-resume-command` | Kiro resume command | return `kiro-cli chat --resume` | Required |\n77\t| `parse-hook` | CLI/IDE hook payloads | map CLI stdin JSON or IDE env-based input to lifecycle events | If hooks capable |\n78\t| `install-hooks` | `.kiro/agents/entire.json`, `.kiro/hooks/*.kiro.hook`, `.vscode/settings.json` | install both CLI and IDE support in one operation | If hooks capable |\n79\t| `uninstall-hooks` | reverse hook installation | remove Entire-owned CLI and IDE hook files plus trusted commands | If hooks capable |\n80\t| `are-hooks-installed` | config presence check | true when either CLI hooks or IDE hooks are present | If hooks capable |\n81\t| `get-transcript-position` | transcript length | CLI uses history entry count; IDE uses history count from cached JSON | If transcript analyzer |\n82\t| `extract-modified-files` | transcript tool-use history | parse tool calls and file edits from cached transcript | If transcript analyzer |\n83\t| `extract-prompts` | user prompt history | return prompt text from transcript history | If transcript analyzer |\n84\t| `extract-summary` | last assistant response | return the final assistant response text | If transcript analyzer |\n85\t\n86\t## Selected Capabilities\n87\t| Capability | Declared | Justification |\n88\t|-----------|----------|---------------|\n89\t| hooks | true | Kiro has both CLI hook config and IDE hook files |\n90\t| transcript_analyzer | true | Kiro transcripts are JSON and can be parsed for prompts and file changes |\n91\t| transcript_preparer | false | the adapter only needs to read cached transcripts, not pre-process live files |\n92\t| token_calculator | false | the worktree adapter does not expose a token-counting path |\n93\t| text_generator | false | Kiro's CLI is used for agent execution, not metadata generation |\n94\t| hook_response_writer | false | the adapter does not depend on structured hook responses |\n95\t| subagent_aware_extractor | false | the worktree code does not model a subagent transcript tree |\n96\t\n97\t## Gaps & Limitations\n98\t- Kiro CLI and Kiro IDE do not share the same native storage format, so Entire must normalize them into `.entire/tmp/<session-id>.json`\n99\t- `kiro-cli` is not the right binary for headless support; the adapter uses `kiro-cli-chat` because it supports device-flow or SIGV4-based non-interactive use\n100\t- The CLI transcript is only reliable at turn end because Kiro's SQLite conversation record is populated late\n101\t- IDE prompt input may arrive through environment variables instead of stdin, so hook parsing must tolerate empty stdin\n102\t- CLI transcript capture now uses an embedded SQLite driver instead of the `sqlite3` shell command, so CLI-native transcript lookup no longer depends on an external binary being installed\n103\t"}]},"uuid":"4652fe39-23c1-4c9e-80e1-03fb4fa624e5","timestamp":"2026-05-04T22:33:19.140Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/kiro-windows-bugs/agents/entire-agent-kiro/A