{"parentUuid":"7e43c463-54c9-4851-b5e2-ea741ae18cd1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UTMPXqrgUhm99ppnYNv66g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Same command on every OS — the only thing that changes is you must be **inside a git repo** when you run it.\n\nFull sequence from a fresh PowerShell window:\n\n```powershell\n# 1. Make sure git works\ngit --version\n\n# 2. Create and enter the test repo\ncd C:\\\nmkdir test-kiro\ncd test-kiro\n\n# 3. Initialize the repo\ngit init\ngit config user.email \"test@example.com\"\ngit config user.name  \"Test\"\n\"hello\" | Out-File -Encoding ascii readme.md\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"init\"\n\n# 4. Make sure external agents are enabled in Entire's settings\nentire settings set external_agents enabled\n\n# 5. Enable kiro in this repo\nentire enable kiro\n```\n\nThat's the whole flow. After step 5 succeeds you'll have new files in `.kiro\\agents\\`, `.kiro\\hooks\\`, and `.vscode\\`.\n\n**Common errors at step 5:**\n\n| Error | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `not a git repository` | You skipped step 3 or `cd`'d out of `C:\\test-kiro` — `cd C:\\test-kiro` and retry |\n| `external_agents is not enabled` | Run step 4 |\n| `'entire' is not recognized` | New PowerShell window needed, or `C:\\Tools` fell off PATH |\n| `kiro: agent not found` / `no external agents discovered` | Run `where.exe entire-agent-kiro` to confirm it's on PATH; if missing, redo the copy to `C:\\Tools` |\n| Interactive prompt (TUI menu) | Use arrow keys to highlight `kiro`, press Space to select, Enter to confirm |\n\nPaste whatever it prints (the success output or the exact error message) and we'll move to the verification step."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":865,"cache_read_input_tokens":80907,"output_tokens":749,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cach