{"parentUuid":"afb8e397-5a05-4974-9cfe-cbb685b1f52d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0187EwS7oHUXmQCiKn2pV4mR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Entire settings file lives **per-repo** at `<repo>\\.entire\\settings.json`. So on Windows for your test repo it's `C:\\test-kiro\\.entire\\settings.json`.\n\nHere's how to do it manually:\n\n```powershell\n# Make sure you're in the repo\ncd C:\\test-kiro\n\n# Create the .entire folder\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path .entire | Out-Null\n\n# Write settings.json with external_agents enabled\n@'\n{\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"external_agents\": true\n}\n'@ | Out-File -Encoding ascii .entire\\settings.json\n\n# Verify\ntype .entire\\settings.json\n```\n\nThen check the agent shows up:\n```powershell\nentire agent list\n```\n\n**If kiro still doesn't appear**, the most likely cause is the binary itself failing the `info` probe. Test it directly:\n```powershell\nentire-agent-kiro info\n```\nThat should print a JSON blob describing the agent. If it errors instead — paste the error.\n\n**Other things to verify:**\n```powershell\n# Binary on PATH\nwhere.exe entire-agent-kiro\n\n# Run with debug logging to see why discovery is skipping it\n$env:ENTIRE_LOG_LEVEL = \"debug\"\nentire agent list 2>&1 | Out-File C:\\test-kiro\\debug.log\ntype C:\\test-kiro\\debug.log\n```\n\nPaste:\n1. Output of `entire-agent-kiro info`\n2. Output of `entire agent list` after creating settings.json\n3. The debug.log if it's still missing\n\nThat'll narrow it down fast."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":638,"cache_read_input_tokens":85079,"output_tokens":1844,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":638,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"ou